  "query_preview": "..\n(Friday night through next Wednesday) \nIssued at 121 PM CST Wed Nov 11 2026\n\nFriday night into Saturday an upper level trough will approach West \nCentral Texas from the west. This will bring our next chance of \nshowers and thunderstorms to the area on Saturday. Low to medium (20-\n50%) rain chances are forecast across the area. Highs on Saturday \nwill be cooler due to the expected cloud cover and possibly rain. \nHighs will be in the mid to upper 60s with overnight lows in the \n50s. The next upper level trough is then forecast to dive southeast \nacross the Southern Plains on late Saturday into Sunday. This will \nbring our next chance of rain Saturday night into Sunday. Low to \nmedium (20-70%) rain chances are forecast for this time frame. Highs \non Sunday will be in the upper 60s to near 70. \n\nA cold front will track south across the area Sunday night into \nMonday as the aforementioned upper level trough tracks east of the \nforecast area. Expect gusty north winds along with cooler \ntemperatures behind the front. Highs on Monday will be in the mid \n50s to near 60. Overnight lows will be in the 40s. The next upper \nlevel system may approach the area toward the middle of next week, \nwhich would bring our next chance of rainfall.",
